B.i10=new A.D("iconOnly",B.a8,"Glyph-only \u2014 no visible label text. Requires `icon`; the `label` is kept as the button's Tooltip/semantics name (real a11y name, not just a visual hint) rather than dropped. Renders as an IconButton (or its filled/filledTonal/outlined variant, per `variant`) with a fixed 44x44 tap target regardless of `dense`. For a row of controls that can't all fit labeled (e.g. a reader action bar) \u2014 design-real-estate-efficiency, wikipick-0830ui.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hZH=new A.D("selectedWhen",B.W,'Render SELECTED (filled, or the selectedColor/selectedTextColor pinned tokens below when set) when the app state this button sets is the current one \u2014 for action-chain buttons, which setFilter highlighting never covered. Either { selected:"<table>", value:"<rowId>" } (a selectRow selection), { table, id, column, value } (a row field), { setting:"<key>", value } (a board setting, "" = unset \u2014 twinmap-1118), or { mapLayer:"<glmap node id>", layer:"<layer id>" } (a glmap vector layer\'s ACTUAL live visibility, via BoardState.effectiveMapLayerVisible \u2014 the exact source of truth the map itself renders from, so an independent layer-toggle chip can never drift from what the map is showing).',B.l,null,!1)
