B.hFb=new A.D("scopeRowId",B.Q,'priorun-0801 C1: restrict the lane population to CONTAINS-descendants of this row id (literal id or a $-token resolved via resolveFilterToken, e.g. $rowId / $selected:<table>). FAIL-CLOSED: configured-but-unresolved (token has nothing to resolve to yet, e.g. nothing currently selected) scopes to the EMPTY set, never falls back to the unscoped board \u2014 the anti-leak guarantee a per-project lens depends on. Unset (default) = today\'s unscoped behavior. Shows a "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip when resolved; the \u2715 clears the underlying $selected:<table> selection for token scopes.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hQd=new A.D("scopeOptional",B.a8,'priorun-0802: opt-in relaxation of scopeRowId\'s fail-closed default \u2014 DEFAULT FALSE, existing behavior byte-identical (still scopes to empty when configured-but-unresolved; a lens must never leak the whole board just because its scope token has not resolved). Set true ONLY for a user-driven SELECTION-CHIP use (e.g. a global view scoped to "whichever row is currently selected", where unresolved means "nothing selected yet", not "the guard rail leaked"): when true and the token is unresolved, renders the FULL unscoped board with no chip; once the token resolves, behavior is identical to the default \u2014 scoped population + the "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hZ1=new A.D("subtitleMaxLines",B.aS,"dispfb-1018: clamp each card's subtitle (body text) to N lines with an ellipsis (e.g. 3). Absent = unclamped (unchanged). The full text is one tap away (the card opens its item).",B.l,null,!1)
B.i6T=new A.D("editAction",B.W,'dispfb-1018: an explicit EDIT affordance (an "Edit" entry in the card menu) \u2014 `{fn, args}` fired with the card\'s row when the card\'s menu "Edit" entry is chosen. With it set, `action` stays the card-body TAP (e.g. selectRow, navigating the detail panel) and editing is only ever the menu entry. Absent = no Edit entry (unchanged).',B.l,null,!1)
B.hYX=new A.D("limit",B.aS,"dispusab-0804: opt-in TOP-N cap PER LANE \u2014 after scope, filters, sort and lane assignment, each lane renders at most N cards. The PREVIEW idiom: a compact lanes strip on an overview screen beside a button that opens the full Priorities view. Per-lane rather than global, because a global cap would silently empty the later lanes. Unset / <= 0 renders every card (byte-identical to before).",B.l,null,!1)
B.hYd=new A.D("colorColumn",B.L,"Optional per-card colour column (a value the engine resolves as a ramp name or #hex).",B.l,null,!1)
