B.hQ0=new A.D("columns",B.kV,'Columns to show (default = all). An entry may be a bare column name OR an object { column, format: currency|percent|compact|number|relative|duration|epochSeconds|epochMillis, decimals?, prefix?, inputUnit?: seconds|millis, style?: date|time|dateTime|relative, valueLabels?: {rawValue: words} (shows words for a raw value, key "" = empty), lines?: 1-6 (wrap long text to N lines), flex?: relative column width, editable?: true, kind?: text|choice|tags, error?: words } \u2014 `format:"check"` (sysmonkit-1127) shows a yes/no value as a centred \u2713 (primary) / \u2013 (grey) with the screen-reader label "<Column>: yes|no"; `editable:true` draws a softly boxed field right in the cell (kind defaults from the column type: enum \u2192 choice, multi-enum \u2192 tags, else text) that saves through BoardState.setField when you leave it or press Enter (Escape cancels), then shows a "Saved \xb7 Undo" notice; a value that fails the column\'s rules shows its message in its own line under the table and is not written. Otherwise a formatted column renders read-only (sorting still uses the stored number). `relative` humanizes an ISO-8601 timestamp column as "3m ago"/"2h ago"/"3d ago"; `duration` shows seconds (or `inputUnit:"millis"`) as a compact localized "3d 4h 12m" / "4h 12m" / "12m 5s" (negative \u2192 "\u2014"); `epochSeconds`/`epochMillis` show a Unix timestamp as localized device-time-zone text, `style` = date | time | dateTime (default) | relative. Non-numeric values pass through untouched.',B.l,null,!1)
B.b4U=new A.D("height",B.Q,'Optional height (scrolls internally). Accepts a number (logical px), "fill" (the full available body height, scrolling/panning internally), or "<frac>fill" (e.g. "0.55fill").',B.l,null,!1)
B.i2Y=new A.D("hideWhenEmpty",B.a8,"Opt-in: render nothing (no empty-state panel) when the table has no rows to show. Unset = the usual empty surface.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hV9=new A.D("pageSize",B.aS,"Opt-in paging (tablepage-1110): show N rows per page with a Previous/Next pager when there are more. The table takes its natural height (ignores `height`) and has NO inner vertical scroller, so the page always scrolls over it. Unset = historic fixed-height body.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hHk=new A.D("rowDetail",B.Q,'Opt-in (tablepage-1110): "readOnly" makes tapping a row open a read-only popup with every shown column in full (no editing, no row action needed). Unset = the row action (or nothing).',B.l,null,!1)
B.dxm=s(["scroll","cards"],t.s)
B.b46=new A.D("overflow",B.bG,'Phone behavior for a grid wider than the pane. "scroll" (default) keeps the grid and scrolls horizontally; "cards" swaps to a stacked card-per-row layout on a phone-width pane (still a grid when wide). Unset = "scroll" (byte-identical to the historic grid).',B.dxm,"Wide-grid overflow",!1)
B.dnX=s(["grid","cards","summary"],t.s)
B.hUh=new A.D("compact",B.bG,'Phone layout (table-phone-cards-1109). `cards` = one card per row: a title cell plus up to three key cells, fixed-set (enum) key cells edited by a dropdown, filter chips built from the values found in the rows with a count each, a Sort menu (default order, name A\u2192Z / Z\u2192A, any column; Group by any enum column in the same menu), a \u22ee menu per row (Open, `openActions`, Edit all fields when the row action is not the editor, then `rowActions`), and tapping a card opens the row (the row `action`, else the record editor). On a wide pane it keeps the grid with the title column pinned (see `stickyKey`). `grid` = the scrolling grid. Absent = `overflow` decides. Wins over `overflow` on a phone. `summary` (sysmonkit-1127) = a calm card per row on a phone: an initial badge, the title, a mono `cardSubtitle` line, a `cardChip` status chip and a trailing \u203a (tap opens the row), then the `cardChecks` as "Web \u2713 Android \u2713 macOS \u2013"; on wider panes it keeps the grid with the title column pinned while the rest scrolls sideways.',B.dnX,null,!1)
B.hXB=new A.D("cardSubtitle",B.kV,'With compact:"summary": columns shown under the title in a mono face, joined by " \xb7 " (e.g. ["id","group"]).',B.l,null,!1)
B.hRf=new A.D("cardChip",B.L,'With compact:"summary": the column shown as a status chip at the card\'s end (its `columns` entry `valueLabels` apply).',B.l,null,!1)
B.hEi=new A.D("cardChecks",B.kV,'With compact:"summary": yes/no columns shown as a row under the title ("Web \u2713 Android \u2713 macOS \u2013"). Default = every format:"check" column.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hJ_=new A.D("periodColumn",B.L,'Opt-in (sysmonkit-1127): a time column (ISO-8601 or Unix epoch) filtered by the screen\'s `period` control \u2014 rows older than the chosen window are hidden; "All" (or no choice) shows every row; a row with no time stays visible. Reads the board setting named by `periodSetting` (default "period"; unset = the control\'s default, 1 day).',B.l,null,!1)
B.hY9=new A.D("periodSetting",B.Q,'With periodColumn: the setting key the `period` control writes (default "period").',B.l,null,!1)
B.hUg=new A.D("hideUnless",B.W,'Opt-in (sysmonkit-1127): {"setting": "showArchived", "column": "archived"} hides rows whose column reads yes while the setting (e.g. a `toggle`) is off; a LIST of such entries applies each.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hZC=new A.D("cardTitle",B.L,'With compact:"cards": the card title column. Default = the first of title/name/label, else the first text column, else the first column.',B.l,null,!1)
B.i6X=new A.D("cardFields",B.kV,'With compact:"cards": the key cells under the title (at most 3). Default = up to three other shown columns, single-choice enum columns first.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hO4=new A.D("filterColumn",B.L,'With compact:"cards": the single-choice enum or reference column whose values become the filter chips (each with its row count; an All chip first). Default = the first enum key cell. `false` hides the chips.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hEK=new A.D("stickyKey",B.a8,'Wide panes: pin the title column while the other columns scroll sideways. On by default with compact:"cards" and "summary"; `false` turns it off, `true` turns it on without cards.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hRa=new A.D("rowActions",B.W,'Per-row \u22ee menu entries for compact:"cards" (same entry shape as the list node\'s `rowActions`: { id?, icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals?, destructive?, hint? } plus builtin "softDelete" / "copy"); a softDelete entry also hides flagged rows.',B.l,null,!1)
B.i4y=new A.D("action",B.W,'Row action spec { fn, args }: tapping a row opens it, and a trailing \u203a (44px, "Open <row name>") at the row end says so. sysmonkit-1127: the table draws NO six-dot grip \u2014 a grip means drag-to-reorder, which table rows do not offer.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hWy=new A.D("filters",B.W,"Column filtering is ALWAYS available on the table (long-press a header to open the shared, type-aware Add-filter editor \u2014 operator picker for text/number, relative/range for dates, is-any-of checklist for enum/reference). The leading header cell clears all filters (tap) and flips AND\u21c4OR combine mode (long-press). Filters are view-only, never persisted. This key is reserved for a future declarative seed.",B.l,null,!1)
B.i6v=new A.D("where",B.W,'Opt-in (dufb-1017), view-only standing scope: {"column": "status", "in": ["done", "superseded"]} (or "equals", or "notIn" to exclude) keeps only matching rows; a LIST of such conditions ANDs them. Header filters still apply on top.',B.l,null,!1)
B.i4z=new A.D("sortBy",B.W,'Opt-in (dufb-1017): default row order {"column": "finishedAt", "descending": true}; rows missing the value sort last.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hVB=new A.D("staleWhen",B.b4,"Name of a SOURCE table this table is derived from (e.g. a `results` table feeding a `metrics` rollup). When the source's newest `updatedAt` is more recent than this table's own newest `updatedAt`, a quiet \"stale \u2014 recalc?\" banner shows above the grid. Unset = no check, byte-identical render.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hOs=new A.D("showProvenance",B.a8,'Show a small read-only "source \xb7 fetched <relative time>" caption above the grid, drawn from the engine-internal provenance envelope auto-stamped by `importData`/`http` when they last landed rows in this table. Unset = no caption, byte-identical render.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hUH=new A.D("openActions",B.W,'Extra compact trailing icon-buttons on each row, each { label, icon?, action } fired with the row injected (e.g. "Show on map" \u2192 focusRow chained with goto). Additive beside the leading row-handle action \u2014 row-tap is unchanged.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hYW=new A.D("scopeColumn",B.L,"Opt-in ENGINE scope filter (see `BoardState.rowsForScoped`) \u2014 the same convention the `explorer` node's `scopeColumn` reads via `activeScope`, so a table bound to a scoped table (e.g. a File > Board > rows chain) shows only the open file/board's rows even when no ancestor explorer for that hop happened to mount. Absent = unchanged behavior.",B.l,null,!1)
