B.hO8=new A.D("traitFilter",B.a8,"Opt-in (njbatch3-1121): Filter opens the Add-filter bar over the rows' traits (tag, group, done, day, repeats, timer), options from the rows present; per device under <settingKey>.traits. Older Show / tag / group filters carry over once.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hKS=new A.D("wideColumns",B.aS,"2 shows groups as cards side by side at 900px and wider; 3 flows them into three columns at 1320px and wider (two from 900px). Default: one list at every width.",B.l,null,!1)
B.i2x=new A.D("timer",B.W,"Opt-in (timers-1108) per-row countdown: { lengthColumn?, endsAtColumn?, leftColumn?, alarm?, presets? } (defaults timerSeconds, timerEndsAt, timerLeft). A row with a length shows m:ss and play; running shows the live time with pause, stop and reset; time's up shows a Stop pill. endsAt is UTC ISO-8601. After each write `alarm` fires with args { op: schedule|cancel, id, title, at }, and once { op: ring, id, title } when a countdown seen running crosses zero. ndfix-1110: savedColumn? (default timerSaved \u2014 \"save for later\" time left, used only when the table has it); restoreAlarms? (true: re-arm running countdowns' alarms once per session, for a cold start); faceColumn? (default timerFace: countdown | countup \u2014 one timer, two faces), elapsedColumn? (default timerElapsed: a stopwatch's banked seconds), track? (true: the time a countdown runs, overtime included, is logged through `tracking`).",B.l,null,!1)
B.i5E=new A.D("tracking",B.W,"Opt-in (timers-1108) per-row time tracking: { startedColumn?, totalColumn?, log?: { table, refColumn, startColumn, endColumn, secondsColumn } } (defaults trackStartedAt, trackedSeconds, time_logs(page, start, end, seconds)). Shows the total and a clock button; while running a red dot, the live stretch and pause, which logs the stretch and adds it to the total. An active countdown takes the row's slot first.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hXP=new A.D("subtasks",B.W,'Opt-in subtasks (ndnotes-1109): true or { parentColumn? (default parentId), titleColumn?, doneColumn?, orderColumn?, values?: {\u2026written on each new subtask}, promoteValues?: {\u2026written when reparent makes one top-level}, parentFilter? }. A subtask is a row of the same table whose parentColumn names a live row passing parentFilter, or a subtask itself (ndfix-1110: nesting is unlimited; done/total counts direct subtasks). maxLevels? (njround4-1121): cap a tree at N levels counting the top task; deeper adds/drops are refused.  Subtasks are not listed as their own rows (nor carry); a parent shows done/total. njnest-1111: doneColumn: false (or the node\'s doneColumn: false) \u2014 no ticks, "N inside", plain "- " bullets in Copy as text; titleFromColumn? (default the node\'s).',B.l,null,!1)
