B.hUM=new A.D("pathLabel",B.W,'Opt-in (njclose-1111): localized map overriding the breadcrumb screen-reader label (default "Task path"), e.g. "Entry path".',B.l,null,!1)
B.hKV=new A.D("copyInHeader",B.a8,"Opt-in (njclose-1111): also show a Copy as text button in the page header (default false; the \u22ee menu always has it).",B.l,null,!1)
B.hOb=new A.D("options",B.W,"The rows, in page order \u2014 the composer draftOptions shape (date, time, duration, startNow, single, multi; choices, sub, scroll, style, recentColumn, showCount\u2026).",B.l,null,!1)
B.hQH=new A.D("timer",B.W,"Countdown columns + alarm, as timercard `timer`; false = none.",B.l,null,!1)
B.i0K=new A.D("tracking",B.W,"Tracking columns + log, as timercard `tracking`; false = none.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hTC=new A.D("deleteAsk",B.W,"The delete alert: {title, message, confirmLabel} ({column} placeholders), true = plain wording (default), false = none.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hGo=new A.D("closeOnSave",B.a8,"Default true: Save steps back to the opener.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hL7=new A.D("carry",B.W,"Opt-in carry-through (carry-1108): { startColumn?, doneColumn?, doneAtColumn?, skipIf?: [columns], filter?, label? } or true. An undone row with a start date shows on every day from it on; once done, from start to the doneAt day (no doneAt: the start day only). A set skipIf column (e.g. a time, a repeat) or a row outside filter keeps its own day. Shows a read-only Active span and Done date under the title band for a row that carries.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hVW=new A.D("openAction",B.W,"Opt-in (ndscreens-1110): the action spec that opens a tapped subtask as its own task view (fired with {table, id}); e.g. selectRow + goto. Without it the subtask opens in place.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hL1=new A.D("notesColumn",B.L,"Opt-in (ndnotes-1109): a multi-line Notes field under the title meta, saved with the page. Shown as text with tappable http(s) links (linkify); a tap elsewhere edits at that spot.",B.l,null,!1)
B.i7n=new A.D("updates",B.W,'Opt-in (njbatch3-updates-v2-1121): { table, taskColumn? (taskId), atColumn? (at), textColumn? (text), maxLength? (500) } \u2014 an Updates section under Notes: "Add a quick update" (Enter adds it, dated now) and past updates newest first, each deletable. Each update is its own row of that table (merges by id, deletes sync as tombstones); written at once, one undo step each.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hXC=new A.D("updatesColumn",B.L,'Opt-in (njbatch3-1121): an Updates section under Notes \u2014 "Add a quick update" (Enter adds it, dated now) and past updates newest first, each deletable. Stored as a JSON list in this text column (util/task_updates.dart); written at once, one undo step each.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hW2=new A.D("webAlarmNote",B.a8,"Opt-in (ndtags-1109): on the web build only, a one-line note under the title meta: alarms ring only while this tab is open.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hJE=new A.D("titleLink",B.a8,"Default true (ndnotes-1109): when the title holds a web link, a small open-link button follows the title field.",B.l,null,!1)
B.hZ4=new A.D("subtasks",B.W,'Opt-in subtasks (ndnotes-1109): true or { parentColumn? (default parentId), titleColumn?, doneColumn?, orderColumn?, values?: {\u2026written on each new subtask}, promoteValues?: {\u2026written when reparent makes one top-level}, parentFilter? }. A subtask is a row of the same table whose parentColumn names a live row passing parentFilter, or a subtask itself (ndfix-1110: nesting is unlimited; done/total counts direct subtasks). maxLevels? (njround4-1121): cap a tree at N levels counting the top task; deeper adds/drops are refused.  The page shows a checklist under Notes (+ Add subtask, tick, rename, remove \u2014 written live); Delete takes the subtasks too, as one undo step. njnest-1111: placement? "end" puts the list at the end of the settings panel; heading? (localizable, "{n}" = count) titles it; addLabel? (localizable) names the add line.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hJ4=new A.D("place",B.W,'Opt-in place row (twinmap-1118): { whereColumn, nameColumn? } \u2014 the explorer\'s place line ("Set place\u2026" \u2192 name + map-pin popup) above Delete; writes the open row live, one undo step.',B.l,null,!1)
B.hIz=new A.D("pageTools",B.W,'Page-tools declaration ({ tools: ["place"] }); resolves the place row like the explorer\'s (an explicit `place` wins).',B.l,null,!1)
